# Code owners for the public AgentCreds SDK.
#
# Owners are auto-requested for review on PRs touching the matching paths. This file is
# ADVISORY until branch protection on `main` enables "Require review from Code Owners" -
# see the note at the bottom before turning that on.
#
# Two rules that bite:
#   * LAST matching pattern wins (the opposite of .gitignore). Keep the catch-all first.
#   * A team is silently ignored unless it is visible AND has explicit write access to
#     this repo. `@agentcreds/maintainers` is visible ("closed") with write - verified
#     2026-07-29. GitHub's web view of this file flags unresolvable owners.

# Default owner for everything.
*                     @agentcreds/maintainers

# The file that decides ownership owns itself.
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @agentcreds/maintainers

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Split these out when there is more than one maintainer. Separate teams with the same
# single member add process without adding a second pair of eyes, so they stay commented
# until the people exist. The paths are the ones worth guarding first:
#
#   /agentcreds-core/src/   @agentcreds/security   # crypto primitives, chain verification
#   /conformance/           @agentcreds/security   # cross-language golden vectors
#   /SECURITY.md            @agentcreds/security   # disclosure policy + contact
#   /.github/workflows/     @agentcreds/release    # publish pipelines (supply chain)
#   /deny.toml              @agentcreds/release    # dependency/license policy
#   /Cargo.lock             @agentcreds/release    # pinned dependency graph
#
# The release paths matter independently of code review: the realistic supply-chain
# attack is a contributor with legitimate write access altering the publish workflow,
# not the library source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# DO NOT enable "Require review from Code Owners" while there is a single maintainer:
# GitHub forbids approving your own PR, so the rule would block every PR you open, with
# admin bypass as the only escape. Turn it on when the second maintainer joins.
